  "facts": [
    "Lyshorn Tunnel, stretching 9.3 kilometres, holds the title of Norway's longest motorway tunnel, outlasting all other Norwegian tunnels by a significant margin since its completion in 2023, it has become a benchmark for future tunnel projects across Scandinavia.",
    "Designed with twin tubes, Lyshorn Tunnel accommodates four lanes—two per tube—ensuring smooth traffic flow and safety, while maintaining a strict 100‑km‑h speed limit throughout its 9.3‑km length.",
    "Strategically positioned on the Svegatjørn‑Rådal stretch of E39, Lyshorn Tunnel links the municipalities of Bergen and Bjørnafjorden, streamlining regional travel between western Norway's key urban centres."
  ],
